      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T21:49:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What about \"location in libcore/*\"?\n\nSome arguments in favor of a module based allowlist are\n1. modules can override the baseline file using `lint.baseline_filename` so it might be good to set the granularity at a module level. \n2. there is also nsjail which can change the workspace layout in theory, thus invalidating any logic that depends on module location  \n\nI dont feel too strongly about this at the moment. I am updating the allowlist logic to `location\u003d\u003dlibcore` since a more probable user workflow is adding a new module in libcore/, in which case users would have had to update the allowlist as well. \n\nThe updated implementation does an exact match on `libcore` and not child directories.\nDo you think child directories skip the check as well?",
      "parentUuid": "de1c18ef_6f0dfe66",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3e2bb84fef43e5da76bcdb0012f8fb95d5dfa4b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca95e48e_26bc3884",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-24T11:32:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this covers the existing use-cases, I\u0027m fine with `libcore` root as the exception.\n\nHowever I wonder if you considered the alternative to propagating strict_updatability_linting. It\u0027d be cool if we kept that enabled for libcore, and just not considered NewApi to be an error for libcore. Pedro shared a pointer further up this thread to where NewApi is added as an error. WDYT? They could probably get rid of their baseline files if so.",
      "parentUuid": "b4513a7b_2658dd3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3e2bb84fef43e5da76bcdb0012f8fb95d5dfa4b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba628438_0516cea3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-25T04:47:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It\u0027d be cool if we kept that enabled for libcore, and just not considered NewApi to be an error for libcore\n\nIIUC this CL should achieve that. It removes NewApi from the `disallowed_issues` flags to `lint_project_xml`\n\n```\n# Some flags omitted for brevity\n\n# cmds before\n$ tools/out/bin/lint_project_xml --baseline libcore/lint-baseline.xml --disallowed_issues NewApi\n$ tools/out/bin/lint --baseline libore/lint-baseline.xml\n\n# cmds after\n$ tools/out/bin/lint_project_xml --baseline libcore/lint-baseline.xml # baseline file can contain NewApi now\n$ tools/out/bin/lint --baseline libore/lint-baseline.xml\n```\n\nPedro, does this align with what you had in mind? Or should the `libcore` based logic be moved to\n1. build/soong/java/lint.go\n2. lint_project_xml host tool\n3. lint host tool\n4. somewhere else?",
      "parentUuid": "ca95e48e_26bc3884",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3e2bb84fef43e5da76bcdb0012f8fb95d5dfa4b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
